<title>JAPAN: Nittetsu Mining sees copper output up.</title>
<headline>Nittetsu Mining sees copper output up.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nittetsu Mining said on Tuesday it plans to produce 19,000 tonnes of refined copper in the half-year to March 1997, slightly above the 18,400 tonnes produced in the same period the year before.</p>
<p>The company said it planned 822 kilograms of gold production, up from 581 kilograms, and 3,913 kilograms of silver output, down from 4,470 kilograms.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
